            <ArticleTitle>Host Microbiota Contributes to Health and Response to Disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>317-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Recent studies have revealed that normal microbiota interacts with the host through four mechanisms: the normal microbiome acts as a barrier against pathogens; second, as modulators of the permeability of host mucosa; third, as modulators of energy extraction from, and metabolic utilization of ingested food; and lastly, as modulators of the immune system. An alteration of the normal microbiota increases predisposition of the host to diseases through these four mechanisms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
